// run
// #3009: `${...}` inside a backtick RAW STRING is literal text, not
// interpolation (spec/SPEC.md:245, unchanged) -- pins that behaviour stays
// exactly as it was once the E0098 warning was added alongside it. This is a
// diagnostic, not a semantic change: the program must still compile and run
// and print the raw text unmodified. The warning itself renders to stderr,
// which `// run` does not compare -- see tests/bit/clicmd/cases.bit's
// rawInterpWarningCases() for the pinned diagnostic text and the
// false-positive guard (a bare `$`, a `$foo`, and an unmatched `${` must all
// stay silent).
fn main() {
  println(`The sum is ${1 + 2}`)
}
